# ControlRig Stable Authoring Phase 6 Live Proof

Date: 2026-06-30

This note records the first sample/temp-only live proof for Phase 6 stable
AnimBP binding. The proof used the UE 5.6.1 editor bridge on
`127.0.0.1:55561` and did not promote stable input defaults during that run.

## Command

The editor bridge was launched temporarily with:

```powershell
$Project = (Resolve-Path .\MCPGameProject\MCPGameProject.uproject).ProviderPath
& 'C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6\Engine\Binaries\Win64\UnrealEditor.exe' $Project -unattended -nop4 -nosplash -nosound -NullRHI -UnrealMCPPort=55561
```

Then the binding proof ran:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_controlrig_animbp_binding_bridge.py --stable-fixture --json
```

## Result

The smoke returned `success=true` for:

- `validate_recipe`;
- `build_controlrig_without_binding`;
- `ensure_anim_graph_controlrig_node_sample`;
- `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` reported `skipped=true` because no
  stable fixture input defaults are reviewed yet.

The proof targeted only:

- `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype`;
- `/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/ABP_Piper_StablePrototype_Binding`.

Observed safety evidence:

- `sample_only=true`;
- `dependency_audit_passed=true`;
- `partial_target_modified=false`;
- `save_requested=false`;
- `input_defaults_applied=false`;
- `input_pins_exposed=false`;
- source AnimBP reported `source_modified=false` and
  `source_asset_modified=false`;
- AnimBP compile result reported `success=true`;
- cleanup command reported success.

Follow-up asset existence query through the bridge reported:

```text
/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/ABP_Piper_StablePrototype_Binding exists=false
/Game/_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable/CR_Piper_StablePrototype exists=false
```

## Boundary

This proof did not approve input-default promotion by itself. A later separate
golden input proof was captured for `PiperStable_GlobalStableGate_CTRL=1.0` and
manually reviewed before the binding contract moved to
`input_default_gate.status=reviewed`.

## Reviewed Input-Default Follow-Up

After the manual promotion patch, the same stable fixture smoke was run again:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\smoke_controlrig_animbp_binding_bridge.py --stable-fixture --json
```

The follow-up returned `success=true` with:

- `set_anim_graph_controlrig_input_defaults` success;
- `compile_bound_anim_bp` success;
- `input_defaults_applied=true`;
- `PiperStable_GlobalStableGate_CTRL` exposed with default `1.0`;
- `save_requested=false`;
- `dependency_audit_passed=true`;
- `partial_target_modified=false`;
- cleanup success.

A bridge cleanup assertion then confirmed both `_MCP_Temp/ControlRigStable`
targets no longer existed.
